            "review_title": "Review at Pingu's Burger",
            "review_text": "Feast and Travel\nMuscat, Oman2083 contributions\n1\nOne of the best places in Ho Chi Minh City to get a decent burger and other delicious treats! Great service and location\nApr 2024 • Solo\nI recently visited this eatery tucked away in a picturesque street in Thao dien during my trip to Ho Chi Minh City and it is easily one of the best places in the city to get a burger or other incredibly delicious food items! From the moment you arrive, you’re swept up by the upbeat and relaxed atmosphere that pulls you in and the best part is that the entire team at Pingu’s goes above and beyond to make sure your experience here is incredible! The staff speaks English as well so it’s very easy to get what you want and when you’re visiting HCMC anytime this year, these small details are what you ultimately want when it comes to a satisfying dining experience!\n\nThe location is cozy and it’s a pretty relaxed setting where you can enjoy fries, burgers, shakes and more with friends, family or loved ones and just appreciate simple and delicious food that is reasonably priced as well! Serving sizes were great and the preparation time was quite fast so you get everything relatively quickly! I loved the fact that their food is prepared in a manner that is as health-focused as possible and I think one visit is not enough for such a place which is providing comfort food and good vibes to every diner coming in.\n\nThey have a variety of great deals going on during specific days as well which is an even greater reason to just pop by, whether you live in Ho Chi Minh City or are just visiting. The Double Beef Burger was absolutely amazing and I loved the cook of the patty and the fact that it remained juicy as well. Their buns are definitely top notch as well and all the accompaniments that went into the burger made is super delicious since each individual flavour shone through and complemented each other perfectly! It was a generous portion in itself and what made it even better was a proper serving of the most deliciously golden french fries whose seasoning you can pick as well (Garlic or spices etc). I think this is absolutely worth going for since they really do make sure you don’t feel even a little hungry after finishing this giant burger!\n\nThe Breakfast Hot Dog is also not your typical hot dog where most places skimp out and aren’t as generous with either the serving portion or the condiments. This hot dog was not only gigantic, it consisted of several individually delicious components that came together to create the most satisfying and tasty hot dog you’d find around here! I also really loved the jolly nature of every team member at Pingu’s and the effortless way they interact and serve diners with ease. Their home made vanilla ice cream that is also sugar free was just too good to be true and is surely one thing I wish I had a much larger version of available back home since it was so refreshing, healthy and absolutely guilt-free! Their menu can be browsed through their posters and they have several choices when it comes to burgers and fries. Overall, I think this is absolutely one place you should not miss when you are in Vietnam because it isn’t quite easy to find an eatery that checks off so many positive aspects when it comes to finding a place to eat that can guarantee no disappointment when it comes to flavours, price points, location and ambiance!\nRead more\nWritten April 26, 2024",
